bridge the system bus into the guest, the way the session bus already is

The guest has no system bus, so a client that asks NetworkManager anything
fails before it starts. Steam is the visible case: its network manager logs
"failed to create a NMClient: Could not connect: No such file or directory" on
every start, and Big Picture shows the network as missing.

The session bus bridge is the model. The host offers /run/dbus/system_bus_socket
on one more vsock port, guarded on the socket existing, and the guest proxies it
to system_bus in the user's runtime directory. The guest init runs as the user
by then and cannot create /run/dbus, so the launchers name the socket through
DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS, which GDBus and libdbus both read.

Upstream: none yet; it builds on muvm-bridge-dbus.patch for DBUS_SOCKET.

